First, fix $n$ large enough, such that the bound of Condition~\ref{cond:X2}\eqref{cX2:Huber} holds, the pseudo parameter of Lemma~\ref{lemma:pseudo} exists and the bound of Lemma~\ref{lemma:pseudoBound} applies. Fix $\mathbb M\in\mathsf{M}_n$ and ${\mathbb P}_n\in\mathbf{P}_n^{(\mathrm{bin})}(\tau)$. Since $H_{\mathbb M,n}(y,\beta) =$ \linebreak $X_n[M]'D_{\mathbb M,n}(y,\beta)X_n[M]$, for a diagonal matrix $D_{\mathbb M,n}(y,\beta)$ whose $i$-th diagonal entry is given by 
$$
-y_i\ddot{\phi}_1(X_{i,n}[M]\beta) - (1-y_i)\ddot{\phi}_2(X_{i,n}[M]\beta)\;>\;0,
$$
in view of Conditions~\ref{cond:H}(\ref{cH:cdf},\ref{cH:concave},\ref{cH:C2}), we see that $H_{\mathbb M,n}^*(y)$ is positive definite. Moreover, from continuity and positivity of $-\ddot{\phi}_j$, $j=1,2$, Lemma~\ref{lemma:pseudoBound} and finiteness of $\mathcal H$, we conclude that the diagonal entries of $D_{\mathbb M,n}(y,\beta_{\mathbb M,n}^*({\mathbb P}_n))$ are lower and upper bounded by positive constants that depend only on $\tau$ and $C$. This finishes the claim in \ref{l:Hcont:A}. Consider now
\begin{align}
&\sup_{\beta\in N_{\mathbb M,{\mathbb P}_n,n}(\delta)} \|H_{\mathbb M,n}^*(y)^{-1/2} H_{\mathbb M,n}(y,\beta) H_{\mathbb M,n}^*(y)^{-1/2} - I_{m(\mathbb M)}\| \notag\\
